  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ukuthula: Women building peace in communities : A Centre for Mediation in Africa project University of Pretoria, South Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Traditional leaders are the backbone of the rural and peri-urban landscape of South Africa, not only in facilitating the delivery of essential services to millions of people, but also in ensuring peace and security in societies torn apart by the legacies of the past and current governance failures. 
This is a 2 year project (March 2024 to February 2026) which has a  particular focus on women traditional leaders, addressing their unique challenges which includes the disconnect between them and key stakeholders at the provincial and national government levels. In addition to this, the project will train 40 women peacebuilders from across the country prior to the 2024 South African elections, in order to equip them with  with the skills to identify signs of emerging conflict and develop actionable and timely responses.</narrative>
  </description>
